# Career Command Center — personal data is NEVER tracked.
#
# Every file below is populated by a session with real personal data: your
# name, salary expectations, work authorization / immigration status, the
# companies you are applying to, and the names of recruiters and interviewers
# (other people's personal data, which is not yours to publish).
#
# Each ships as a `.example` template that IS tracked. `bootstrap.sh` copies
# each example to its live filename on first run; the live file stays ignored.
# That is the same example -> local pattern the parent repository uses for its
# sanitization lexicon, and for the same reason: the template is safe to
# publish, the populated file never is.
#
# A comment saying "do not commit this" is not a control. This file is.

profile.yml
GOALS.md
_Logs/session-log.md
job-search/applications-tracker.md
job-search/target-companies.md
interview-prep/star-stories.md
interview-prep/interview-retro.md
career-strategy/compensation-strategy.md
career-strategy/positioning-narrative.md
career-strategy/90-day-plan.md

# Résumé and cover letter output — almost always contains name, address,
# phone, and email.
*.docx
*.pdf
resume-*.md
cover-letter-*.md
!templates/resume-template.md
!templates/cover-letter-template.md
